               TrackStm Version 1.0 - Release Notes
               ===================================

Program Description
-------------------

Hurricane Tracking program for Psion 3a and compatible computers.


Platforms
---------

 This program runs on PSION S3a and ACORN PocketBook II computers.


Installation
------------

1) Unzip the downloaded TRACKSTM.ZIP to your local PC.
2) Create the following subdirectories on your Psion's
   Default Disk (you can tell your currently assigned
   Default Disk by hitting the Shift-Psion-H keys from the
   main Psion menu.
            \TRACKSTM
            and
            \TRACKSTM\TRACKS
3) Using PsiWin, RCOM, or equivalent, transfer TRACKSTM.OPO to
the \OPO directory.  Transfer GULF.PIC to \TRACKSTM


Operation of TrackStm
---------------------
Run TrackStm through selecting TrackStm under the OPL icon
from the main Psion menu, then hitting the Enter key.

The first time TrackStm is run, it will not find any
storm files within the \TRACKSTM\TRACKS directory, so it
will automatically prompt you to enter a storm name.
The default file will be "Gigantic.dbf".  You may choose
any name so long as you adhere to the 8-character limit
of the psion for the main name, and use the ".dbf" extension
to signify the file type.

After entering the file name, you will be in the main
TrackStm screen, which provides just three options:

   1) See the Hurricane
   2) Edit Storm's Data
   and
   3) Exit

Since the first time TrackStm is run you will not have any data
present in the storm file, you should probably initially choose
option 2.  Upon choosing this option, you will be in a data
entry screen where-in you should enter the first data point
of the storm.

Information requested will be Date (of the data point), time,
latitude (N), longitude (W), and maximum recorded wind speed.

After entering this information, you should select "C" to C)opy
(i.e. append) this record to the storm data file.  Note that
if you make a mistake before selecting "C", you can hit the
Escape key to abort this screen and to return to the main
menu.

Repeat the above steps for as many data points as you have.  When
you are finished, either hit Escape from the data entry screen,
or hit "N" for N)ext record, and you will be returned to the
main menu.

To see the storm at this point, select option 1.  You will
then see the map of the Gulf of Mexico, and on the right and bottom
corner of the screen will see "Any Key to Advance Storm."

Following these instructions, kit a key to see the first and
second data points displayed.  Note that you will now continue to
see the "Any Key to Advance Storm" notice, but will also see an
echo of the data that you had previously provided for the second
data point.

Repeat this until you see the final data point, at which you will
see an indication of this with the message "The Storm Plot is Finished."
Hit any key to return to the main TrackStm menu.

At this point you may wish to Edit the storm track data, or add
additional points.  To edit, again choose option 2) from the
menu.  Simply select "N" for N)ext record until you come to the
record that you wish to edit.  At this point, make the editing
modifications, then select N)ext so that the modified changes
are stored.

On the other hand, if you wish to add a new data point (note that
added data points do NOT need to be chronologically AFTER the
latest point, but may actually be between or even before existing
data points.  To do this, enter the new data over any
record's displayed information, then hit "C" for C)opy.

Again, you can terminate your editing at any point by either
hitting Escape, or selecting N)ext until the final record is
displayed.

To edit, select again option 2) from the main

